[Music]  let's talk about classic chrome  [Music]  recently i made two new sony film  simulations one is a replica after the  fujifilm classic chrome film simulation  and the other one is a picture profile  made after the original kodachrome 64  film stock and in this video i'll  explain in detail the main  characteristics and differences between  the fujifilm and the sony classic chrome  let me know in the comments if you want  to find out more about the kodachrome 64  film simulation and i'll make another  video about it before we start remember  all sony film simulation recipes can be  found on my website  let's start with the classic chrome  this sony picture profile was made after  the fujifilm simulation and i used the  fuji xs10 to compare the two sample  clips as you can see they look very  similar with some slight differences  they are identical in terms of contrast  fuji seems to have a better dynamic  range but with worse noise performance  and in terms of color it's about 90  matching which is a pretty good result  taken into consideration i was able to  do this in camera only with the use of  the picture profile settings  as you can see the sony is much much  cleaner and has more details than the  fuji which seems pretty muddy  because of the light gathering  capabilities of the sony a73 the sensor  captures about a stop more light than  the fuji  so i had to lower down the exposure by  one stop to match the brightness in the  two cameras which again will give the  sony much cleaner results and has a  clear advantage here  unfortunately with the cine1 game on  sony the dynamic range seems to be a  little bit lower than the fuji at first  glance but one thing to remember is that  the cine1 gamma is the low light profile  and has 109 output which means you can  recover 9 of the print highlights and  i'll show you exactly what i'm talking  about  as you can see in this image it seems  like the highlights are completely blown  out but if we start to recover the  highlights and the shadows we can see  that it actually contains more detail  and has higher dynamic range than  initially seemed like and remember this  is only 8-bit on 10-bit cameras you'll  have a better color rendition and even  less noise  you could set the profile to cd4 to  increase the dynamic range inside the  camera but the noise performance lowers  considerably and the colors shift a lot  especially the yellow shift towards  green and skin tones towards pink which  for me personally is a big no-no  in theory the c4 skin tones can be  easily corrected in camera just by  lowering the color face to let's say -2  and that will shift the reds a little  bit more towards orange but that will  change the whole color spectrum shifting  the yellows even closer to green and i  honestly just don't like that for a look  from my experience the yellow is the  most problematic of all colors  especially on the sony's that's why some  companies like canon choose to  desaturate their yellows inside the  camera to run their perfect skin tone  also fun fact  yellow doesn't even exist at least not  how we see it  the human eye can only capture colors of  red blue and greens yellows and magentas  are actually generated by the brain  if you don't mind the color shifting of  the c4 you can definitely use it instead  of cine one for higher dynamic range but  only in well-lit conditions  in low light situations i find the cd4  to be quite noisy without applying some  noise reduction so besides that let's  take a closer look at the colors  the sony reds are shifted towards pink  while fuji is more orange the sony  greens are more olive while fuji greens  are shifted towards cyan and the yellows  are very close fuji being shifted  towards orange while sony looking more  accurate real life the rest of the  colors are more or less identical  overall i would rate this profile 90  identical to the fujifilm and you know  we were really paying close attention to  the color differences but when shooting  in a real-life situation it might not  even be that obvious we still get really  nice colors out of the camera  but still let's bring it even closer to  the fujifilm colors and i'll show you  exactly how to further adjust it in  davinci resolve for a perfect match  so in the color tab in the hue versus  hue menu shift the red stores orange  next take the greens and shift them just  a little bit towards cyan  now drag the yellows just a little bit  towards orange  [Music]  and finally shifted cyan  [Music]  now let's see the final result  it's almost indistinguishable to save  you some time i will upload this slot on  my website so you can download it for  free  that's pretty much all i want to show  you about the classic chrome let's move  on to the quarter chrome 64 a film stock  that is more interesting to me and that  is because replicating the quarter  chrome 64 was without any doubt my most  difficult and biggest challenge of  replicating any film stock  let me know in the comments if you want  me to talk about the kodachrome 64 film  simulation and i'll make a video about  it till next time have fun and take care  see ya  [Music]

